b895bae0-a22e-5a6a-874e-7b72daf60f3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-74084" :question/problem "Given the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$, which of the following vectors are orthogonal to $u?$\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We compute the dot product between $u$ and each of the listed vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =4+0+0-4 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {w}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {w}_{4} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-4)+(-1)\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-8-1+0+3 \\\\  & =-6.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot x & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {x}_{4} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot 3+(-3)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =0-3+6-3 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the correct option is $v$ and $x$ only." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74084/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce8958e6-c578-572f-8b34-5513b6f64a51"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74084"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74089/selection/bfbf91f109f6c4c7b8242ca2b1bf4bae476945344d0e5e07bf789ea29825342a" :answer/id #uuid "36830d78-8c3e-5983-9655-f98090bb4d77" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$v$ and $w$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74089/selection/c697a5dc7422c431e6e3043f66b73fae4a68a519aa87f9d288564a9d244fdfef" :answer/id #uuid "d1b71968-f0e7-5eb1-9b2f-7d51c86afa4a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/v