993/selection/c286394386ae9fb6724e458b654d34895a2465038e1d8d690ba0010ee69c36e5" "q-39993/selection/0ebaf08027b4114197f45f0e21c6b2a594c4b80e081fff923c98396f7b258619"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39993" :question/id #uuid "b9a92f4f-4161-5159-b146-a1cb45d4ca87" :question/math-academy-id "q-39993" :question/problem "Given the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, which of the following vectors are orthogonal to $u?$\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We compute the dot product between $u$ and each of the listed vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot (-7)+8\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =5-7+16-15 \\\\  & =-1.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {w}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {w}_{4} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot (-5)+8\\cdot (-1)+(-3)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =15-5-8-6 \\\\  & =-4.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot x & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {x}_{4} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-1)+8\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-5-1+8-12 \\\\  & =-10.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the correct option is 'None of the listed'." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-39993/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce8958e6-c578-572f-8b34-5513b6f64a51"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39993"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39988/selection/b8a2ff73faa89fd963b5996730ce3ee1add64186fab4840199e529152fa385d6" :answer/id #uuid "1b9dc96a-2577-5d0c-b850-80934c791d9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-2,5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39988/selection/b552fda7f0f1aace343d10d4d0d3239e5033799e33a5b6c76d831738f490dc67" :answer/id #uuid "ed757a9e-d2a8-54de-854a-4f3828047f86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39988/selection/338eec5434d358c375f2a346c343b4ffdb61443daf8dabde8fd69f15bcd32c95" :answer/id #uuid "b0aa2eaa-8921-559a-a5d8-013c2e673062" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-3,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39988/selection/9703321249450988ea64127cf8e92b0dc2edb1ab309ebcd7f3209f0829b242dc" :answer/id #uuid "af5052e3-396d-59df-bae0-a31cbab91f53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-1,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39988/selection/0f9c3928feb9e10db3cfa6067cf8de1b42b30bd40d8bee6d8b0f1ea306f7fd22" :answer/id #uuid "2b22576c-4852-59f7-b576-f7c35f935b23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39988/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bfe8be23-0f85-5291-b431-766a7b21e14d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-39988/selection/9703321249450988ea64127cf8e92b0dc2edb1ab309ebcd7f3209f0829b242dc" :answer-field/choices ["q-39988/selection/b8a2ff73faa89fd963b5996730ce3ee1add64186fab4840199e529152fa385d6" "q-39988/selection/b552fda7f0f1aace343d10d4d0d3239e5033799e33a5b6c76d831738f490dc67" "q-39988/selection/338eec5434d358c375f2a346c343b4ffdb61443daf8dabde8fd69f15bcd32c95" "q-39988/selection/9703321249450988ea64127cf8e92b0dc2edb1ab309ebcd7f3209f0829b242dc" "q-39988/selection/0f9c3928feb9e10db3cfa6067cf8de1b42b30bd40d8bee6d8b0f1ea306f7fd22"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39988" :question/id #uuid "cb8b8f76-e901-5830-b1da-cc88f2a31e41" :question/math-academy-id "q-39988" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -k\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ k \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that  $u⊥v.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ and $v$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that their dot product is equal to zero.\nFirst, let's calculate the dot product in terms of $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =k\\cdot k+(-5)\\cdot k+(-1)\\cdot 3+(-k)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & ={k}^{2}-5k-3+3k \\\\  & ={k}^{2}-2k-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the dot product to zero, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2}-2k-3 & =0 \\\\ (k-3)(k+1) & =0 \\\\ k & =-1,3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-39988/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ea335d6-6ee6-514f-acd4-deb39d50cf81"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39988"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39324/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer/id #uuid "14b2a881-6b7b-51f8-bce9-ecb43a86bc94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39324/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "ce8eec84-0ae2-5f49-b0cd-d7ab80edf0e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39324/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "fea8cb18-1199-5933-8b61-6f65fd1ef25b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39324/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "51e43284-2d58-512c-8c73-d7463f4f0ca0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39324/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "02563a48-9dcd-5e