n/problem "If $u=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ are orthogonal vectors, then $k=$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ and $v$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that their dot product is equal to zero.\nFirst, let's calculate the dot product in terms of $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =2\\cdot k+(-3)\\cdot 3+1\\cdot (-4)+(-5)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2k-9-4+5 \\\\  & =2k-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the dot product to zero, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2k-8 & =0 \\\\ 2k & =8 \\\\ k & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74092/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ea335d6-6ee6-514f-acd4-deb39d50cf81"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74092"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74093/selection/22628916ea1c486fb54556a9f8d8d61355d92c8ea728bad7ba526d2caa1cce91" :answer/id #uuid "432fda16-cf5e-5024-beee-34714bb97e39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=0,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74093/selection/f9a36dc20554097250ff0324e179977bb892219ae9b27b5c2ca8864aac6c0450" :answer/id #uuid "c0bc277c-bbee-5e3a-8943-0eef7326ef5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74093/selection/8d79a93119a22b1b29da9c471aea477570c48f78d0ecaccf107fdb60453c5bbc" :answer/id #uuid "52e73195-a543-56df-a1e9-dfa3077e7fdc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-2,0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74093/selection/a9d809426690fc6065e8673c85a555723d4ab72d745ec39834681473e579f93a" :answer/id #uuid "9059c385-9e12-549e-955f-f7b0badc7ecb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74093/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb9