]} {:db/id "q-140123" :question/id #uuid "6462a8a7-0592-5fe5-81e2-36fc28907977" :question/math-academy-id "q-140123" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}3k \\\\ -6 \\\\ k \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that  $u⊥v.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ and $v$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that their dot product is equal to zero.\nFirst, let's calculate the dot product in terms of $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =k\\cdot 3k+1\\cdot (-6)+3\\cdot k+(-2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =3{k}^{2}-6+3k+0 \\\\  & =3({k}^{2}+k-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the dot product to zero, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({k}^{2}+k-2) & =0 \\\\ 3(k+2)(k-1) & =0 \\\\ k & =-2,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140123/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ea335d6-6ee6-514f-acd4-deb39d50cf81"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140123"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-39333"] :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that $u\\,⊥\\,v.$ Find $(v+w)\\cdot u+v\\cdot (u+w).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ and $v$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that $u\\cdot v=0.$ Therefore, using linearity of the dot product to expand the parentheses, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v+w)\\cdot u+v\\cdot (u+w) & =v\\cdot u+w\\cdot u+v\\cdot u+v\\cdot w \\\\  & =0+w\\cdot u+0+v\\cdot w \\\\  & =w\\cdot u+v\\cdot w \\\\  & =((-3)\\cdot 3+2\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & +(2\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 5+(-1)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =(-9-4+5+4)+(-6+8+0+2) \\\\  & =-4+4 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-74181/selection/23c0b4da815e7ba954fedc5e75955047cfe471feec4d2029849a63511c000fa3" :answer/id #uuid "69e5bfa3-21b6-5514-9b0c-1c30fbcf1a51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74181/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "f0ebc4f7-0b0e-5b95-a283-0a52c898f36d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74181/selection/ac46d580a95a8fc03d1a7cb07de70e107b73fba6bf1bc1d13103b84eff3df012" :answer/id #uuid "3cdb5a21-4674-5af3-9c62-0777a73343be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "17" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74181/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer/id #uuid "80f78e2e-858f-5f4f-9641-d20e2c7d5b0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74181/selection/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279" :answer/id #uuid "e95446f7-4be9-5905-9fed-969562662944" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74181/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "469c5318-397a-5add-b681-9ea48166156d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74181/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer-field/choices ["q-74181/selection/23c0b4da815e7ba954fedc5e75955047cfe471feec4d2029849a63511c000fa3" "q-74181/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" "q-74181/selection/ac46d580a95a8fc03d1a7cb07de70e107b73fba6bf1bc1d13103b84eff3df012" "q-74181/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" "q-74181/selection/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74181" :question/id #uuid "df5ce87c-4049-5f98-86f3-21fa4e066b4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74181" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that $u$ and $v$ are orthogonal. Find $(2u+3w)\\cdot v+u\\cdot (v-w).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ and $v$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that $u\\cdot v=0.$ Therefore, using linearity of the dot product to expand the parentheses, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2u+3w)\\cdot v+u\\cdot (v-w) & =(2u)\\cdot v+(3w)\\cdot v+u\\cdot v-u\\cdot w \\\\  & =2(u\\cdot v)+3(w\\cdot v)+u\\cdot v-u\\cdot w \\\\  & =0+3(w\\cdot v)+0-u\\cdot w \\\\  & =3(w\\cdot v)-u\\cdot w \\\\  & =3(0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot 1) \\\\  & -(0\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =3(0+2+0+-2)-(0-1-9-4) \\\\  & =0-(-14) \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-74181/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc757fa2-12ce-5a1c-a524-8eb256842079"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74181"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74180/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "e9d74241-bf94-59c0-8dee-9547d62ddabc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74180/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "86979ed9-b31d-5f4c-b9a2-cd2130c295fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74180/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "cd5ecf5a-2fd1-5153-9849-e18c6bcd8ef1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/valida